# steps/named-struct-exec.md §12: a field declared in a block of a named Structure's body is the block's,
# as in a method's body -- it lives in the procedure's occurrence, with the block, not in the Structure
# (no path `Counter\t`).  t is 5, added to n: n 5 after each of two executions (n's declaration runs
# again); twin, a method with the same body, reads 5.  Entry 7.
Counter:
    size_t: n 0U
    if: n = 0U
        size_t: t 5U
        n: n + t
return
fn: twin () size_t
    size_t: n 0U
    if: n = 0U
        size_t: t 5U
        n: n + t
return: n
Counter
size_t: a 9U
a: Counter\n
Counter
size_t: b 9U
b: twin()
int: ok 0
if: a = 5U && Counter\n = 5U && b = 5U
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
